---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const question = "Do drylined walls need to be skimmed?";
const answer = `Not always. There are four recognised levels of plasterboard finish under BS 8212:

- Level 0 - Unfinished (no jointing)
- Level 1 - Joints tape-and-bedded only (typical behind tiles)
- Level 2 - Joints filled, no finish on board face
- Level 3 - Tapered-edge boards tape-and-jointed, ready for textured paint
- Level 4 - Taped-and-jointed or skimmed, ready for flat emulsion
- Level 5 - Premium full skim, defect-free surface for gloss or critical lighting

Most Maidstone residential work lands at Level 4 — either tape-and-jointed with a quality jointing compound, or skimmed with a 2-3mm plaster skim. Commercial fit-outs in Maidstone riverside and the office parks around Maidstone town centre often use a full skim for the cleanest visual under office LED lighting.

Skim adds £7 - £11 per m² in Maidstone but eliminates any visible board joint telegraphing through paint.`;
const description = `Not always. There are four recognised levels of plasterboard finish under BS 8212:  - Level 0 - Unfinished (no jointing) - Level 1 - Joints tape-and-bedded only`;
const canonical = "/drylining-faq/do-drylined-walls-need-to-be-skimmed/";

const schema = {"@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [{"@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "Do drylined walls need to be skimmed?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Not always. There are four recognised levels of plasterboard finish under BS 8212:\n\n- Level 0 - Unfinished (no jointing)\n- Level 1 - Joints tape-and-bedded only (typical behind tiles)\n- Level 2 - Joints filled, no finish on board face\n- Level 3 - Tapered-edge boards tape-and-jointed, ready for textured paint\n- Level 4 - Taped-and-jointed or skimmed, ready for flat emulsion\n- Level 5 - Premium full skim, defect-free surface for gloss or critical lighting\n\nMost Maidstone residential work lands at Level 4 — either tape-and-jointed with a quality jointing compound, or skimmed with a 2-3mm plaster skim. Commercial fit-outs in Maidstone riverside and the office parks around Maidstone town centre often use a full skim for the cleanest visual under office LED lighting.\n\nSkim adds £7 - £11 per m² in Maidstone but eliminates any visible board joint telegraphing through paint."}}]}, {"@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://dryliningmaidstone.co.uk/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "FAQ", "item": "https://dryliningmaidstone.co.uk/faq/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Do drylined walls need to be skimmed?", "item": "https://dryliningmaidstone.co.uk/drylining-faq/do-drylined-walls-need-to-be-skimmed/"}]}]};---

<Layout
  title={question + " | Drylining Maidstone"}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  schema={schema}
>
  <main class="container" style="padding: 34px 0 70px;">
    <article class="card" style="padding: 28px; max-width: 860px;">
      <header style="margin-bottom: 22px;">
        <p style="margin: 0 0 10px; color: var(--primary); font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 13px;">
          Maidstone Drylining FAQ
        </p>
        <h1 style="margin: 0; font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 36px); line-height: 1.15;">{question}</h1>
      </header>

      <section style="padding: 18px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom: 22px;">
        <p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">Not always. There are four recognised levels of plasterboard finish under BS 8212:</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">- Level 0 - Unfinished (no jointing)
- Level 1 - Joints tape-and-bedded only (typical behind tiles)
- Level 2 - Joints filled, no finish on board face
- Level 3 - Tapered-edge boards tape-and-jointed, ready for textured paint
- Level 4 - Taped-and-jointed or skimmed, ready for flat emulsion
- Level 5 - Premium full skim, defect-free surface for gloss or critical lighting</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">Most Maidstone residential work lands at Level 4 — either tape-and-jointed with a quality jointing compound, or skimmed with a 2-3mm plaster skim. Commercial fit-outs in Maidstone riverside and the office parks around Maidstone town centre often use a full skim for the cleanest visual under office LED lighting.</p>
<p style="margin: 0 0 1rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--text);">Skim adds £7 - £11 per m² in Maidstone but eliminates any visible board joint telegraphing through paint.</p>
      </section>

      <section style="margin: 24px 0; padding: 18px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border);">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 12px; color: var(--text);">Related Questions</h3>
        <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
<li><a href="/drylining-faq/what-is-the-difference-between-dry-lining-and-plastering/" style="color: var(--primary); font-weight: 500;">Difference between dry lining and plastering</a></li>
<li><a href="/drylining-faq/can-dry-lining-improve-wall-insulation/" style="color: var(--primary); font-weight: 500;">How much does dry lining cost in Maidstone?</a></li>
<li><a href="/services/taping-and-jointing/" style="color: var(--primary); font-weight: 500;">Tape and jointing service</a></li>
